@ 42 - Uralic
# citation: The following reconstructed phonology for Proto-Uralic is adapted from the Wikipedia: For the series of changes starting with Proto-Uralic to Pre-Finnic and ending with Proto-Finnic to Livonian and in several other of Tropylium’s contributions, the following alterations to the stand-in variable list apply. Tropylium wishes to note that his sound changes are subject to change. (Note 2014/06/21: As per a Tumblr post of his, http://tropylium.tumblr.com/post/81916666722/index-diachronica-4-2, many of the compilations presented here are out of date or erroneous, and he still is updating his page on Finnic, http://www.frathwiki.com/Finnish.) (From Wikipedia contributors (2011), “Proto-Uralic language”. Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia. <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Proto-Uralic_language>; the TCL thread and KQ pages proper; and Tropylium.)